Id: dbs007f
Severity: FAIL
Category: services
Check: check_databases
Fix: Make it postgres's alone: chown postgres:postgres, chmod 700.
References: postgresql.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 3.3; NIST AC-3, SC-28; ISO 8.3; CE Secure configuration

PostgreSQL's data directory can be read by accounts that should never
see it. It holds every table, and the server itself refuses to start
when its permissions are this open, which says what it thinks of them.
